#! clause: L11.2
#! mode: run
#! expect-out: x
#! expect-out: x
# A `do … end` block passed to a block-consumer procedure imported from another module (L§8.5 +
# L§11.2): invoking `body()` inside `twice` runs the caller's block in its own context. `lib`'s
# first proc `greet(name)` is present so a regression that reads the block against the *consumer's*
# module (lib) would mis-resolve to `greet` and raise `missing-argument` for `name`.
import lib.*
twice() do
    print("x")
end
